{"title":"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Problems 8, 9 and 10 use the data found in the accompanying paragraph and figures\n</p><p>Four friends, Art, Roger, Paul and Trisha, bake cookies, and all cookies have the same thickness. The shapes of the cookies differ, as shown.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Art's cookies are trapezoids: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30c19e251320f614c89dd05c7666eb4b5b8eb84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(5,0)--(5,3)--(2,3)--cycle); draw(rightanglemark((5,3), (5,0), origin)); label(&quot;5 in&quot;, (2.5,0), S); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (5,1.5), E); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (3.5,3), N);[/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Roger's cookies are rectangles: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffcf7138f4fa79b3d3030ad4a0e82a3a03322bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(4,0)--(4,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw(rightanglemark((4,2), (4,0), origin)); draw(rightanglemark((0,2), origin, (4,0))); label(&quot;4 in&quot;, (2,0), S); label(&quot;2 in&quot;, (4,1), E);[/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Paul's cookies are parallelograms: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb7278165b0333733d86c18cdd642361a580edc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(3,0)--(2.5,2)--(-0.5,2)--cycle); draw((2.5,2)--(2.5,0), dashed); draw(rightanglemark((2.5,2),(2.5,0), origin)); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (1.5,0), S); label(&quot;2 in&quot;, (2.5,1), W);[/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Trisha's cookies are triangles: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da492eba3c75cd91135085acf373c1215d7f5b48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(3,0)--(3,4)--cycle); draw(rightanglemark((3,4),(3,0), origin)); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (1.5,0), S); label(&quot;4 in&quot;, (3,2), E);[/asy]\" width=\"122\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p>How many cookies will be in one batch of Trisha's cookies?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f234ed655fef8242a897aa1eca5c863754a17b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Art's cookies have areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f61f2cea25a0dca8ff4d177b8cf597a8ef36f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 3 + \\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{2}=9+3=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" />. There are 12 cookies in one of Art's batches so everyone used <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/1788cccfea911cf25341832065b9759d1e25bca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot 12=144 \\text{ in}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" /> of dough. Trisha's cookies have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8b910c54297cd8d71b32edba58294c8765e066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\cdot 4}{2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" /> so she has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d379f538395b656a3f06df6b38c4e4c0ffc92cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{6}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" /> cookies per batch.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the same method as the previous solution you can find that Art's cookies have a area of 12 and Trisha's cookies have an area of 6. Because they both used the same amount of dough and Trisha's cookies use half the dough compared to Art's you can just multiply the total number of cookies Art makes by 2 to balance out the dough used. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a2f9c72944d664505c5f0f032b6542e3995d3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b3104f61320b27432b8494542a5b28de9b01a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8\">2003 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" 